    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 200', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp 200', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1\\n##\\n\\nThis includes:\\n1. Enabling BGP with AS 200 (matches both Juniper's global AS and peer AS in this case)\\n2. Configuring the IPv6 BGP neighbor\\n3. Setting the local update source address (equivalent to Juniper's local-address parameter)\\n4. Note: The export policy would need separate route-map configuration in Cisco\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 200'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1\\n##\\n\\nThis includes:\\n1. Enabling BGP with AS 200 (matches both Juniper's global AS and peer AS in this case)\\n2. Configuring the IPv6 BGP neighbor\\n3. Setting the local update source address (equivalent to Juniper's local-address parameter)\\n4. Note: The export policy would need separate route-map configuration in Cisco\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 remote-as 200\\n neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1\\n##\\n\\nThis includes:\\n1. Enabling BGP with AS 200 (matches both Juniper's global AS and peer AS in this case)\\n2. Configuring the IPv6 BGP neighbor\\n3. Setting the local update source address (equivalent to Juniper's local-address parameter)\\n4. Note: The export policy would need separate route-map configuration in Cisco\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 2001:db8:100::2 update-source 2001:db8:100::1'}]]": 1,
    "['term [parameter2] from protocol [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map EXPORT-POLICY permit 10', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 200'], 'root': 'router bgp 200', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT-POLICY permit 10\\n match protocol connected\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper\\'s `policy-statement` translates to Cisco\\'s `route-map`\\n- `term 1` translates to sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses increments of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` translates to `match protocol connected` (Cisco uses \"connected\" instead of \"direct\" for directly connected routes)\\n- The implicit `then accept` in Juniper translates to `permit` in Cisco\\'s route-map', 'trans_template': 'route-map EXPORT-POLICY permit 10'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match protocol connected', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 200'], 'root': 'router bgp 200', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper policy statement:\\n\\n##\\nroute-map EXPORT-POLICY permit 10\\n match protocol connected\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper\\'s `policy-statement` translates to Cisco\\'s `route-map`\\n- `term 1` translates to sequence number `10` (Cisco typically uses increments of 10)\\n- `from protocol direct` translates to `match protocol connected` (Cisco uses \"connected\" instead of \"direct\" for directly connected routes)\\n- The implicit `then accept` in Juniper translates to `permit` in Cisco\\'s route-map', 'trans_template': 'match protocol connected'}]]": 1,
